---
source: crates/leptoskit_db_schema/tests/diff.rs
expression: "format!(\"{}\\n{}\", postgres.validate().unwrap_err(),\nsqlite.validate().unwrap_err())"
---
the schema has 12 problem(s):
  - sequence Bad Name: the name `Bad Name` must be lowercase snake case (a-z, 0-9, _), starting with a letter or _
  - sequence posts: another object in the schema has the same name
  - function live.forged: the body doesn't match its checksum; regenerate the schema rather than editing it
  - function live.quoted: the body can't contain `$leptoskit$`, which quotes it
  - trigger on_nothing on missing: its table isn't in the schema
  - trigger copies on posts: `copies` names `missing`, which isn't a column
  - trigger dup on posts: another trigger has the same name
  - constraint trigger early on posts: only a Postgres trigger that runs after the write can wait for the commit
  - trigger idle on posts: a trigger needs at least one event
  - trigger lost on posts: it calls `live.missing`, which isn't in the schema
  - trigger statements on posts: Postgres triggers call a function
  - trigger twice on posts: UPDATE is listed twice

the schema has 5 problem(s):
  - sequence numbers: SQLite has no sequences
  - function live.capture: SQLite has no functions
  - trigger both on posts: a SQLite trigger fires on one event
  - trigger calls on posts: SQLite triggers run statements, not functions
  - trigger same on users: another trigger has the same name
